<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brocken</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brocken is the highest mountain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> range in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, rising to 1,141 metres. Wrapped in fog for much of the year, it is famed in German folklore as the gathering place of witches on Walpurgis Night, a scene used by Goethe in Faust. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> it lay in the East German border zone and housed Soviet and East German listening posts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brocken.jpg" alt="Brocken" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Axel Hindemith · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brocken_vom_Torfhaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
